{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "09", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "03", "M": "28", "S": "04"}}, "news": [{"title": "Jaypee homebuyers\u2019 complaints genuine, Suraksha Group breached resolution plan: Panel", "para": "An independent committee examining Jaypee Infratech homebuyers\u2019 grievances has found most allegations of construction delays, poor quality, labour shortages and fund diversion to be genuine. The committee said Suraksha Group had failed to meet key resolution-plan obligations, including arranging Rs 3,000 crore in working capital, and urged urgent tribunal intervention.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/jaypee-homebuyers-complaints-genuine-suraksha-group-breached-resolution-plan-panel/134805365?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-77258/134805365.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Gurugram: Residents oppose DLF plan to install 24 DG sets near Moulsari Avenue metro station", "para": "In Gurgaon, residents of a local housing society are voicing strong objections to the installation of diesel generators in their vicinity. These installations, claimed to have been erected without proper environmental clearances, have sparked worries about pollution and safety risks. Developers argue that the generators do not necessitate specific approvals, yet residents raise concerns about their closeness to a metro corridor.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/gurugram-residents-oppose-dlf-plan-to-install-24-dg-sets-near-moulsari-avenue-metro-station/134805329?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-52698/134805329.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Over 39,800 rural families get pucca houses in Uttarakhand under PMAY-Gramin", "para": "Since 2022, a total of 39,815 rural families in Uttarakhand received pucca houses under the Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana-Gramin. Udham Singh Nagar led with 4,882 houses built, followed closely by Haridwar and Rudraprayag with significant contributions. The state government has sought additional housing allocations from the Centre to continue supporting the initiative. Under the scheme, eligible beneficiaries receive direct financial assistance for effective housing construction.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/over-39800-rural-families-get-pucca-houses-in-uttarakhand-under-pmay-gramin/134805288?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-99388/134805288.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}]}